$\int \frac{d x}{2^x-1}=\int \frac{d x}{\frac{1}{2^{-x}}}=\int \frac{2^{-x}}{1-2^{-x}} \cdot d x$
Let $1-2^{-\mathrm{x}}=\mathrm{t} \Rightarrow 2^{-\mathrm{x}} \cdot \log 2=\frac{\mathrm{dt}}{\mathrm{dx}}\begin{aligned}
& \Rightarrow 2^{-\mathrm{x}}=\frac{1}{\log 2} \cdot \frac{\mathrm{dt}}{\mathrm{dx}} \Rightarrow 2^{-\mathrm{x}} \cdot \mathrm{dx}=\frac{\mathrm{dt}}{\log 2} \\
& \therefore \int \frac{2^{-\mathrm{x}}}{1-2^{-\mathrm{x}}} \mathrm{dx}=\frac{1}{\log 2} \int \frac{\mathrm{dt}}{\mathrm{t}}=\frac{1}{\log 2}(\log \mathrm{t})+\mathrm{c} \\
& =\frac{1}{\log 2}\left(\log \left(1-2^{-\mathrm{x}}\right)\right)+\mathrm{c}
\end{aligned}$
